        "title": "fix(store): order hydration observations durably",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- order canonical thread and revision observations by lossless RFC3339Nano source time plus a durable pre-fetch sequence\n- reject delayed hydration payloads before they can overwrite canonical threads or dependent comments, PR details, documents, and evidence\n- apply the same schema-aware freshness contract to summaries, embeddings, clustering, and archive coverage while preserving read-only legacy archive support\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./...`\n- `go test -race ./internal/store ./internal/syncer`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `make generate-sqlc` followed by a clean diff\n- Gitcrawl Store portable/hydration test suite against the branch binary\n\n## Exact-head real migration proof\n\nValidated at `7ac705a98269de4ccd5c382909b9a394372a7b66`:\n\n- built the released `v0.7.1` source at `10725cf8aa5daba9f8714a6774b2f7ddcaabc1e6` and created a real schema-4 SQLite archive with repository, PR, revision, file, and workflow-run rows\n- opened that archive through the PR-head write path: `pragma user_version` advanced to `10`, `pragma integrity_check` returned `ok`, diagnostics reported `current`, and all seeded rows survived\n- verified legacy observations remain sequence `0` while the schema-10 child reservation constraint excludes `workflow_runs` and the separate repository/head-SHA workflow table exists\n- simulated supported-schema compatibility drift by setting persisted observation high-water marks to `19` and deleting the allocator table; reopening rebuilt the allocator floor at `19` with integrity `ok`\n- reran the delayed-parent/completion and overlapping-sync adversarial store/syncer tests `20` times successfully\n",
